We need to translate: "Obinna na-enwe mmasị ịgaghari n'akụkụ paaki ógbè, nke dị akụkụ anọ were dị 550 mailụ n'ụzọ 175 mailụ isi. Ọ bụrụ na ọ na-aga mailụ 50/awa, kedụ awa ole ọ na-emefu were a ga ije?" It's Igbo language. Let's translate: "Obinna likes to walk around the perimeter of a rectangular park, which has sides 550 meters and 175 meters. If he walks at 50 meters per hour, how many hours will it take him to walk around?" Wait: "n'akụkụ paaki ógbè" means "around the perimeter of a park". "dị akụkụ anọ were dị 550 mailụ n'ụzọ 175 mailụ isi" means "which has four sides of 550 meters and 175 meters" maybe? Actually "dị 550 mailụ n'ụzọ 175 mailụ isi" maybe "with sides 550 meters and 175 meters". So rectangle with length 550 m and width 175 m. He walks at 50 m per hour. How many hours to walk around? So compute perimeter: 2*(550+175)=2*725=1450 meters. Speed 50 m/h. Time = distance / speed = 1450/50 = 29 hours. Wait 1450/50 = 29. So answer 29 hours. But check units: meters? Actually "mailụ" maybe "meters". So 29 hours. Provide final answer numeric: 29. Let's produce reasoning.assistantfinalFirst find the perimeter of the rectangular park.  
The park has two sides of 550 m and two sides of 175 m.

\[
\text{Perimeter}=2(550+175)=2(725)=1450\text{ m}
\]

Obinna walks at a speed of 50 m per hour.  
The time required to walk the entire perimeter is

\[
\text{Time}=\frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Speed}}
          =\frac{1450\text{ m}}{50\text{ m/h}}
          =29\text{ h}
\]

So Obinna will need **29 hours** to walk around the park.
